"""Publish only after corrected replay and statistical audit have passed."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json,re
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent; P=R/'Saved Model/stage2_comparison_study_v2'
read=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text())
a=read(P/'analysis_summary.json'); audit=read(P/'audit_complete.json'); tests=read(P/'correction_tests.json'); run=read(P/'summary.json')
assert audit['passed'] and tests['passed']
stats=a['arm_statistics']; contrasts=audit['all_contrasts']; primary=contrasts[0]; dist=a['paired_contrasts'][0]['distance_difference']
labels={'rules_only':'Rules-only construction','minimum_change':'Minimum-change projection','model_guided':'Model-guided search'}
table='| Method | Completed | Numerical pass | All-check accepted | Median runtime (s) | Median normalized change |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n'
for key,label in labels.items():
    s=stats[key]
    table+=f"| {label} | {s['completed']}/100 | {s['numerical_pass']}/100 | {s['overall_accepted']}/100 | {s['runtime_seconds']['median']:.3f} | {s['distance_from_observed']['median']:.4f} |\n"
conclusion=f"Model-guided search accepted {stats['model_guided']['overall_accepted']}/100 profiles versus {stats['minimum_change']['overall_accepted']}/100 with minimum-change projection and {stats['rules_only']['overall_accepted']}/100 with rules-only construction. The primary paired difference was {primary['difference_pp']:+.2f} percentage points (10,000-resample percentile bootstrap 95% CI {primary['ci_pp'][0]:+.2f} to {primary['ci_pp'][1]:+.2f}); the exact two-sided discordance test gave p={primary['exact_p']:.7f} ({primary['wins']} wins, {primary['losses']} losses). This is a model-score acceptance result, not demonstrated health improvement."
displacement=f"The paired mean additional normalized displacement for model-guided search was {dist['point_diff']:.4f} (bootstrap 95% CI {dist['ci_lower']:.4f} to {dist['ci_upper']:.4f}). The scales are fixed engineering weights; this does not measure meal acceptability."
report='# Stage 2 three-method comparison: corrected evidence v2\n\nUpdated 23 November 2026. Post-result correction on the same 100 participants; this is not an independent replication cohort. Original v1 results and document copies are preserved.\n\n## Methods and scope\n\nAll arms share participant inputs, baseline calibrated predictions for routing, energy prescriptions, nutrient envelopes and final score gate. Rules-only refers to target construction without model-guided search, not a model-free pipeline. Its exact values are project reference policies and must not be represented as uniformly established clinical guidelines. Minimum-change projects observed nutrients; model-guided runs the existing 50-step search then the same projection. No model assets, routing thresholds, search objective or production engine were changed.\n\n## Corrected results\n\n'+table+'\n'+conclusion+'\n\n'+displacement+'\n\n'
report+='## Corrections and verification\n\n- Removed duplicate Adam execution from the timing runner. The saved pre-projection vector now comes from the actual search used for the final target.\n- Applied 1e-6 absolute tolerance in nutrient units to all Filter 2 inequalities in the versioned comparison checker. Case 49 previously failed because 0.7999999999999999 was compared strictly against 0.8 g/kg. The historical production diagnostic remains archived in per-arm audits; authoritative comparison decisions use the corrected common checker. Production code itself is unchanged.\n- Replaced bootstrap tail proportions with exact paired binary tests. Corrected the distance confidence interval to bootstrap the paired mean rather than reporting percentiles of individual differences.\n- Fresh model replay checked all 300 outputs, baseline probabilities and immutable features. The verifier shares deployed preprocessing and a numerical-check helper; statistical/distance calculations were independently reproduced from saved vectors and records.\n'
report+=f"- Seven targeted correction tests passed. Maximum target change versus v1: {audit['max_target_difference_from_v1']:.9g}; changed overall acceptance decisions: {audit['acceptance_changes_from_v1']}.\n"
report+=f"- Actual run device: {run['device']}; GPU: {run['gpu']}; PyTorch CPU threads: {run['torch_threads']}. Timings include baseline inference and candidate evaluation, exclude model loading, and use CUDA synchronization and an untimed inference warm-up. Fixed arm order and one timing run limit performance claims. The old 5.74-second and 28.5-fold figures are superseded.\n\n"
report+='## Paired acceptance contrasts\n\n| Contrast | Difference (pp) | Pointwise bootstrap 95% CI (pp) | Exact p | Secondary Bonferroni-adjusted p |\n| --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n'
for c in contrasts:
    adj='Not applicable' if c['secondary_bonferroni_p'] is None else f"{c['secondary_bonferroni_p']:.7g}"
    report+=f"| {c['contrast']} | {c['difference_pp']:+.2f} | [{c['ci_pp'][0]:+.2f}, {c['ci_pp'][1]:+.2f}] | {c['exact_p']:.7g} | {adj} |\n"
report+='\nPrimary acceptance contrast uses alpha .05. Two secondary acceptance contrasts use Bonferroni correction; their displayed 95% intervals are pointwise, not simultaneous. Other endpoints are exploratory. Statistical corrections were made after reviewing v1 results and are disclosed as amendments.\n\n## Limits and next step\n\nThe acceptance gate is self-referential: the prediction model also guides optimization. Neither clinical benefit nor Indian prediction validity is established. Continuous nutrient feasibility does not ensure a realizable meal. Zeroed or independently assigned nutrient components in the rules-only construction are engineering targets, not a demonstrated food composition. No cascade was deployed or prospectively tested. Next: a matched Stage 3 translation study using frozen food data, constraints, objectives and solver budgets.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n`Saved Model/stage2_comparison_study_v2/` contains protocol.json, cases_LOCAL.json, 300 checkpoints, summary.json, analysis_summary.json, paired_contrasts.csv, correction_tests.json, verification.json and audit_complete.json. The latter verifies full paired intervals, exact tests, numerical counts, distances and timing summaries. Source scripts are versioned with v2 suffixes.\n'
(R/'Research Paper/Stage2_Comparison_Study_v2.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
old=R/'Research Paper/Stage2_Comparison_Study_v1.md'
old.write_text('# Historical Stage 2 comparison v1 — superseded\n\nThe original report is preserved at `Saved Model/stage2_comparison_study_v2/original_document_copies/Stage2_Comparison_Study_v1.md`. Raw v1 results remain unchanged. Use [corrected v2 report](Stage2_Comparison_Study_v2.md) for current conclusions. Corrections address duplicated optimization timing, a rounding-only numerical failure, confidence intervals, exact paired tests and verification scope.\n',encoding='utf-8')
note='STAGE 2 COMPARISON CORRECTION v2 — 2026-11-23\n'+conclusion+'\n'+displacement+'\nAll 300 corrected executions completed; full model and statistical verification passed. Numerical acceptance uses the documented tolerance. Timings are from a single-search rerun; see the v2 report for measured values. Earlier v1 runtime/p-value claims are superseded. Original study artifacts are retained. Report: Research Paper/Stage2_Comparison_Study_v2.md. Evidence: Saved Model/stage2_comparison_study_v2/.\n\n'
for name in ['Progress.txt','Current_Model_Explanation.txt']:
    p=R/name; text=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'); marker='STAGE 2 REPAIR CORRECTION AND REGRESSION'
    assert marker in text
    p.write_text(note+text[text.index(marker):],encoding='utf-8')
p=R/'Research Paper/Readiness_and_Evidence.md'; text=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'); marker='## Stage 2 repair correction'
assert marker in text
p.write_text('## Corrected Stage 2 comparison — 23 November 2026\n\n'+note.split('\n',1)[1]+text[text.index(marker):],encoding='utf-8')
p=R/'Research Paper/BioNutriGPT_Manuscript_v2.md'; text=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'); start=text.index('### 3.3 Stage 2 Comparative'); end=text.index('### 3.4 Historical optimizer',start)
replacement='### 3.3 Stage 2 comparative added-value study (corrected v2)\n\nA post-result corrected evaluation reran the same 100 reserved complete-input temporal NHANES profiles across three target-construction methods. All methods used common model-informed routing and envelopes. The amendment removed duplicate search from timing, aligned floating-point checks and corrected inference statistics; it did not change model assets or the optimization objective.\n\n'+table+'\n'+conclusion+'\n\n'+displacement+'\n\nAll methods passed numerical checks in the corrected evaluation. The v1 minimum-change exception was floating-point rounding, not meaningful protein inadequacy. Fresh model replay and separate statistical recomputation verified 300 records. The primary exact test is unadjusted; secondary acceptance tests use Bonferroni adjustment and other endpoints remain exploratory. Timings describe one fixed-order run, not a controlled hardware benchmark. These findings do not establish clinical benefit, Indian validity or discrete meal feasibility. See Stage2_Comparison_Study_v2.md and Saved Model/stage2_comparison_study_v2/audit_complete.json.\n\n'
p.write_text(text[:start]+replacement+text[end:],encoding='utf-8')
print(conclusion);print(table)
